    "expTypeList": {
      "type": "any[]",
      "description": "Expenditure types for the grid's Expenditure Type column, as a PLAIN ARRAY (not a vb/ArrayDataProvider2 -- VBCS tracks an ADP by reference, so reassigning one breaks the binding). getExpTypeProvider() in the page module wraps it and falls back to the four values PROVEN accepted by unprocessedProjectCosts when this is empty, so the picker is never blank. Fill it per page load with the list Fusion returns for the request's project, the same call the Post Cost drawer and the PR drawer make: ProjectLOV/getFscmRestApiResources11_13_18_05ExpenditureTypes with finder=ValidValuesFinder;flex_vst_bind3=<ProjectId>. Items are {value,label} keyed on the type NAME, because the OIC map sends _EXPENDITURE_TYPE_ID_Display.",
      "defaultValue": []
    },
    "expTypeMap": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Which expenditure types were AUTHORED for each equipment master, keyed by master id: { <masterId>: { level: 'MASTER'|'SUBCLASS'|'CLASS'|'NONE', types: [{value, isDefault, displayOrder, useCount}] } }. Narrows the Expenditure Type picker per ROW, from the project's whole list (84 on dev20) to the two or three that belong to that equipment -- which cannot be derived from names (measured: 3 of 569), so it is authored in EQR_EXP_TYPE_MAP and read back. Filled from eqp-v1/resolveExpTypeMaps by the enter and week-refresh chains; see resources/js/expenditureTypes.js loadMapsForMasters(). REASSIGN the whole object rather than adding keys in place -- VBCS tracks it by reference and the pickers will not re-render otherwise (the same reason expTypeList is a plain array). An empty map, a missing master, or level 'NONE' all mean \"not authored\", and the picker then keeps the full list: never blank it, or the user cannot record their week.",
      "defaultValue": {}
    },
    "internalRequestId": {
      "type": "number",
      "defaultValue": 0,
      "description": "Internal eqrEquipmentRequestId, resolved at page enter from the request NUMBER (this page only ever receives the number). Needed because patchRequestLine is PATCH /equipment-requests/{requestId}/lines/{id} and takes BOTH ids - without this the per-line expenditure-type save 404s on every attempt while looking like a working implementation. Resolved via expenditureTypes.resolveRequestIdByNumber, which uses views/workbench-requests and asserts the returned row matches: equipment-requests?requestNumber= declares the parameter and ignores it, returning the oldest of 368 rows."
    }
  },
